(p) to appoint members to various Authorities in accordance with the provisions of 
the Act; 

(q) to propose drafts of Statutes for submission to the Board of Governors; 
(r) to regulate the conduct and discipline of the students of the University; 
(s) to take actions necessary for the good administration of the University in general 
and to this end exercise such powers as are necessary; 
(t) to delegate any of its powers to any Authority or officer or a committee; and 
(u) to perform such other functions as have been assigned to it by the provisions of 
